6.2 Transaction-style commands

Implement local transaction behaviour to the extent reasonably possible.

Support:

* COMMIT
* ROLLBACK
* SAVEPOINT

These commands must have clearly documented local semantics.

A suitable implementation is to stage mutations in a working copy of the local database state until COMMIT, while displaying the working results inside the console.

On COMMIT:

* Validate the complete pending change set.
* Apply all accepted changes to the shared local state.
* Persist the result.
* Refresh the website’s derived data.
* Clear the committed transaction log.

On ROLLBACK:

* Discard uncommitted mutations.
* Restore the transaction’s initial working state.
* Do not overwrite previously committed local changes.

On SAVEPOINT:

* Save the current transaction snapshot.
* Allow rollback to a supported named savepoint if implemented.

Do not call local browser-storage changes a real Oracle transaction.

If complete transactional semantics cannot be implemented safely, implement a simpler consistent model and document the limitation.

